1
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:03,959
Get in.

2
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:51,080
Hello, President Wen.

3
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:53,080
Hello, President Xia.

4
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:01,199
Hello, President Wen.

5
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:15,080
Hello, President Wen.

6
00:03:25,879 --> 00:03:26,919
Stop.

7
00:03:26,919 --> 00:03:27,759
Stop right there.

8
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:37,960
I thought you'd never make it back.

9
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:40,240
What did the people in Taipei say?

10
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:43,000
Who did you meet on this trip back?

11
00:03:43,159 --> 00:03:43,919
Did they say anything about

12
00:03:43,919 --> 00:03:45,919
why they separated us for the polygraph test,

13
00:03:45,919 --> 00:03:47,319
and even kept you an extra day?

14
00:03:47,319 --> 00:03:48,599
That has never happened before.

15
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:54,319
If you keep acting like this, saying nothing,

16
00:03:54,840 --> 00:03:56,960
we'll both be in danger if we fail the polygraph test.

17
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:59,439
You have no idea what those people are capable of.

18
00:03:59,439 --> 00:04:01,240
But I don't know what you're capable of either.

19
00:04:01,919 --> 00:04:03,360
What are you trying to say?

20
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:04,759
What are you really up to?

21
00:04:04,759 --> 00:04:06,479
If I wanted to do something, I'd have done it already.

22
00:04:10,319 --> 00:04:12,719
Listen to me, now isn't the time to throw a fit.

23
00:04:12,719 --> 00:04:14,960
You must tell me what happened on your trip to Taipei,

24
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:16,439
in full detail.

25
00:04:16,439 --> 00:04:18,279
Don't leave out a single detail.

26
00:04:18,279 --> 00:04:18,600
Otherwise...

27
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:19,439
I'm not afraid.

28
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:20,959
Are you?

29
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:30,759
Flirting and entertaining guests—

30
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:32,600
we run an entertainment venue.

31
00:04:32,879 --> 00:04:34,360
Having pretty girls around is normal.

32
00:04:34,680 --> 00:04:35,800
If you need company,

33
00:04:36,319 --> 00:04:37,639
I can arrange the girls for you,

34
00:04:37,639 --> 00:04:39,680
because I know who's safe.

35
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:41,079
But Wen Zongshu,

36
00:04:41,519 --> 00:04:42,839
fooling around is one thing,

37
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:44,800
but at your age,

38
00:04:45,120 --> 00:04:46,759
you actually caught real feelings?

39
00:04:46,959 --> 00:04:47,920
Come on, Haohao.

40
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:49,800
Come here. Walk forward.

41
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:51,040
Careful, watch your step.

42
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:53,439
Watch your step. Good boy! Haohao, come here.

43
00:04:53,439 --> 00:04:55,079
Come here. Let's play on the slide.

44
00:04:55,079 --> 00:04:56,399
Play on the slide with Mommy.

45
00:04:56,399 --> 00:04:57,319
Down the slide!

46
00:04:57,680 --> 00:04:58,279
Good!

47
00:04:58,600 --> 00:04:59,360
The ball!

48
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:09,480
You went over to someone else's house

49
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:11,319
to babysit their kid and cook for them?

50
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:14,639
Have you no shame?

51
00:05:18,079 --> 00:05:19,720
If you wanted a son,

52
00:05:21,519 --> 00:05:23,000
you should've told me sooner!

53
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:35,720
If you settle this matter properly,

54
00:05:37,079 --> 00:05:38,759
I can be a stepmother to this child.

55
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:41,360
We can't just think about the present.

56
00:05:42,160 --> 00:05:42,920
What about the future?

57
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:46,279
When you turn 70,

58
00:05:47,279 --> 00:05:48,160
what will you do then?

59
00:05:54,439 --> 00:05:57,120
I told you not to keep calling me.

60
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:59,480
I didn't answer because I was in the middle of talks.

61
00:05:59,920 --> 00:06:00,959
We're at the hospital.

62
00:06:00,959 --> 00:06:02,199
The child is delirious with fever.

63
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:04,519
It could be laryngitis—that can be fatal.

64
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:06,560
Wait a moment.

65
00:06:10,959 --> 00:06:11,759
Mr. Zhu.

66
00:06:13,879 --> 00:06:14,680
When are you leaving?

67
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:16,360
Tomorrow.

68
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:20,600
Chief Wei.

69
00:06:21,959 --> 00:06:22,839
Dessert.

70
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:25,279
How thoughtful of you.

71
00:06:26,879 --> 00:06:28,720
Wen Zongshu and Sister Xia have fallen out.

72
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:29,879
Word just came in.

73
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:32,040
Taiwan, China hasn't made any moves for now.

74
00:06:33,959 --> 00:06:36,079
Could they be silenced?

75
00:06:36,720 --> 00:06:38,639
At least there's a chance they'll flee back to Taiwan, China.

76
00:06:38,639 --> 00:06:40,639
Just like Lin Kanshan back then.

77
00:06:42,839 --> 00:06:44,959
As long as Wen Zongshu makes a move to retreat,

78
00:06:45,959 --> 00:06:47,560
arrest him immediately if conditions allow.

79
00:07:30,319 --> 00:07:31,839
The family's acknowledgment.

80
00:07:39,720 --> 00:07:40,360
Old Zhu...

81
00:07:41,839 --> 00:07:42,519
My condolences.

82
00:07:42,839 --> 00:07:43,800
Thank you, Director.

83
00:07:45,199 --> 00:07:45,839
My condolences, ma'am.

84
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:46,720
Thank you, Director.

85
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:51,199
I'll see you out.

86
00:07:57,879 --> 00:07:58,879
Please stay. Don't see me out.

87
00:07:59,319 --> 00:08:00,199
Thank you, Director.

88
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:14,040
Are your hands still shaking?

89
00:08:14,759 --> 00:08:16,480
Did you forget to take your insulin?

90
00:08:16,680 --> 00:08:18,360
Chen Leyuan has cozied up to the director.

91
00:08:19,399 --> 00:08:20,839
Must be nice to be young.

92
00:08:21,160 --> 00:08:23,000
Scrambling up the ladder pretty fast.

93
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:24,279
Just watch.

94
00:08:24,759 --> 00:08:26,000
I'm about to be pushed out.

95
00:08:27,079 --> 00:08:29,240
Ever since this Ma showed up, you've been risking your life.

96
00:08:29,519 --> 00:08:31,639
I've never seen you drink that much.

97
00:08:32,360 --> 00:08:32,960
Was it worth it?

98
00:08:33,399 --> 00:08:35,159
Not a single drop was for nothing.

99
00:08:36,279 --> 00:08:37,879
If he can truly be of use to me,

100
00:08:38,840 --> 00:08:40,279
it's worth drinking myself into the ER.

101
00:08:40,759 --> 00:08:42,120
He's slippery as an eel.

102
00:08:42,840 --> 00:08:44,399
You think you can keep a hold on him?

103
00:08:44,679 --> 00:08:46,519
I have to try.

104
00:08:46,519 --> 00:08:47,679
How will I know if I don't try?

105
00:08:48,840 --> 00:08:49,519
Take a gamble.

106
00:08:50,279 --> 00:08:51,559
What if you lose?

107
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:53,799
Then I'll retire with honor.

108
00:08:53,799 --> 00:08:55,519
Grow vegetables and cook for you.

109
00:08:55,759 --> 00:08:57,639
But you haven't retired yet.

110
00:08:58,279 --> 00:08:59,840
Those sleeper agents you planted on the mainland...

111
00:08:59,960 --> 00:09:01,159
you'd better keep hold of them.

112
00:09:01,559 --> 00:09:03,039
If they're all rooted out,

113
00:09:03,039 --> 00:09:04,679
you'll be left all alone.

114
00:09:04,679 --> 00:09:06,159
Chen Leyuan won't even need to lift a finger.

115
00:09:06,360 --> 00:09:07,480
You'll knock yourself out of the game.

116
00:09:11,759 --> 00:09:13,279
Hello, I'd like to buy a ticket.

117
00:09:13,399 --> 00:09:14,799
Hello, ma'am. Where to?

118
00:09:15,120 --> 00:09:15,840
Guangzhou.

119
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:17,679
All right, one moment.

120
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:22,720
He's arrived.

121
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:33,919
He's almost through security now.

122
00:09:33,919 --> 00:09:35,360
Any word from the bureau yet?

123
00:09:35,480 --> 00:09:38,200
Is it a normal departure or extraction? Do we arrest him?

124
00:09:38,519 --> 00:09:40,519
The bureau still hasn't given instructions.

125
00:09:40,879 --> 00:09:42,600
Just sit tight and wait for orders.

126
00:09:46,080 --> 00:09:47,799
Is he testing us?

127
00:09:47,919 --> 00:09:49,080
Are we arresting him or not?

128
00:09:55,159 --> 00:09:56,559
That must be the update.

129
00:09:59,639 --> 00:10:02,399
If he actually leaves, arrest him.

130
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:09,919
No need to return for now.

131
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:11,720
Have Sister Xia suspend all operations.

132
00:10:12,120 --> 00:10:13,519
Wait for my word on when to return home.

133
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:48,000
Hey man, how did it go?

134
00:10:53,679 --> 00:10:54,759
We found Great-Aunt.

135
00:11:04,279 --> 00:11:05,440
That's a relief, then.

136
00:11:05,639 --> 00:11:08,399
Your grandpa and dad can both be at peace now.

137
00:11:09,080 --> 00:11:10,840
My dad told me

138
00:11:11,120 --> 00:11:14,080
Grandpa had always waited for Cross-Strait family visits.

139
00:11:14,679 --> 00:11:16,000
He'd wanted to return for so long.

140
00:11:17,240 --> 00:11:20,279
Yet just six months before restrictions were lifted,

141
00:11:20,279 --> 00:11:21,159
he passed away.

142
00:11:22,159 --> 00:11:24,360
In the end, he never made it back.

143
00:11:34,399 --> 00:11:35,279
Great-Aunt.

144
00:11:35,279 --> 00:11:37,279
This is my grandfather, Lin Xiaoxian.

145
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:39,039
My father's name is Lin Zude.

146
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:40,919
Do you remember?

147
00:11:43,759 --> 00:11:45,080
Look at this. Look here.

148
00:11:45,399 --> 00:11:46,240
Look at this.

149
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:47,440
This kid next to him...

150
00:11:47,440 --> 00:11:48,759
do you remember who he is?

151
00:11:50,360 --> 00:11:51,200
Granny.

152
00:11:51,559 --> 00:11:54,000
This is Lin Xiaoxian.

153
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:55,000
Your older brother.

154
00:11:55,639 --> 00:11:57,360
The child beside him...

155
00:11:57,519 --> 00:11:59,039
is Lin Zude.

156
00:11:59,039 --> 00:11:59,919
And this one...

157
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:01,600
is Lin Kanshan.

158
00:12:01,600 --> 00:12:03,360
He's Zude's son.

159
00:12:03,360 --> 00:12:05,399
He came all this way to see you.

160
00:12:06,559 --> 00:12:07,200
I don't remember.

161
00:12:07,600 --> 00:12:08,279
Granny...

162
00:12:08,279 --> 00:12:09,120
She's very old.

163
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:09,960
Right, right.

164
00:12:10,759 --> 00:12:11,519
Comrade,

165
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:14,639
I don't know him.

166
00:12:15,639 --> 00:12:19,159
Our family has no relatives of Taiwan, China spies.

167
00:12:19,559 --> 00:12:22,320
We don't have overseas connections either.

168
00:12:22,519 --> 00:12:23,559
We have nothing like that!

169
00:12:23,960 --> 00:12:26,399
The village chief asked us this morning.

170
00:12:26,799 --> 00:12:28,039
He already inspected everything!

171
00:12:28,279 --> 00:12:29,919
Granny, that's not what this is.

172
00:12:29,919 --> 00:12:30,960
Granny,

173
00:12:31,360 --> 00:12:32,759
you've got it wrong.

174
00:12:32,879 --> 00:12:35,679
I'm Xiao Chen from the township.

175
00:12:35,879 --> 00:12:38,559
I brought him to our village to find his family.

176
00:12:38,919 --> 00:12:40,200
We're not here to catch spies.

177
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:41,879
That's right, Granny. Don't be scared.

178
00:12:41,879 --> 00:12:43,080
Don't worry.

179
00:12:43,519 --> 00:12:44,200
Granny.

180
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:44,799
Don't be nervous.

181
00:12:44,799 --> 00:12:46,000
Don't be afraid.

182
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:53,120
Have some melon seeds.

183
00:12:55,039 --> 00:12:55,799
You have some too.

184
00:12:57,840 --> 00:12:59,639
She's getting on in years.

185
00:12:59,639 --> 00:13:01,559
Sometimes she's lucid, sometimes confused.

186
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:03,399
It's just good that you found her.

187
00:13:03,639 --> 00:13:04,519
It's good that you found her.

188
00:13:04,519 --> 00:13:06,919
Don't leave, Brother!

189
00:13:07,440 --> 00:13:08,799
Brother!

190
00:13:09,480 --> 00:13:10,440
Brother!

191
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:13,279
Brother!

192
00:13:16,759 --> 00:13:17,559
Brother!

193
00:13:18,480 --> 00:13:20,679
Once you left, you never came back.

194
00:13:22,039 --> 00:13:24,600
Father couldn't see you,

195
00:13:25,759 --> 00:13:28,080
and cried until his eyes were ruined.

196
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:30,399
Go tell the army,

197
00:13:30,840 --> 00:13:32,879
tell them you can't hear,

198
00:13:33,200 --> 00:13:34,480
and your legs are bad.

199
00:13:34,559 --> 00:13:35,879
You can't go to Taiwan, China.

200
00:13:35,919 --> 00:13:37,559
You must tell them! Don't keep quiet!

201
00:13:37,559 --> 00:13:39,519
What are you scared of, Brother?

202
00:13:44,039 --> 00:13:44,879
Brother!

203
00:13:45,480 --> 00:13:47,080
They wanted to take you away.

204
00:13:47,480 --> 00:13:50,559
They said they'd shoot you if you didn't go.

205
00:13:51,639 --> 00:13:53,960
No one in our family dared to speak up.

206
00:13:54,279 --> 00:13:55,879
Don't blame Father.

207
00:13:55,879 --> 00:13:58,320
Don't blame him, okay?

208
00:14:01,679 --> 00:14:02,720
Back then,

209
00:14:03,960 --> 00:14:07,799
our whole family had no choice...

210
00:14:07,799 --> 00:14:10,159
but to walk you to the village entrance.

211
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:12,960
On the way there, you told me...

212
00:14:13,360 --> 00:14:15,360
you hadn't eaten and were hungry.

213
00:14:15,559 --> 00:14:18,200
So I hurried back home to get you food.

214
00:14:18,720 --> 00:14:20,639
But the meal wasn't ready yet.

215
00:14:20,840 --> 00:14:23,080
I couldn't wait, so I ran back.

216
00:14:23,080 --> 00:14:25,320
When I got back, the military truck was driving off.

217
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:27,440
And I never saw you again, Brother.

218
00:14:27,440 --> 00:14:30,000
Never again.

219
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:34,159
I kept...

220
00:14:34,879 --> 00:14:38,360
I kept thinking, why did I run back for food?

221
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:41,919
If I hadn't gone home, I could've seen you more.

222
00:14:41,919 --> 00:14:43,720
Instead, I never saw you again.

223
00:14:43,720 --> 00:14:46,039
I never saw you again, Brother!

224
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:50,720
Never again.

225
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:56,279
Brother!

226
00:14:58,720 --> 00:15:04,200
I've lived to this ripe old age,

227
00:15:06,440 --> 00:15:08,360
yet I don't dare to die.

228
00:15:09,159 --> 00:15:11,200
I'm afraid that when you come back,

229
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:13,519
you won't be able to find me.

230
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:15,759
If you don't return,

231
00:15:16,240 --> 00:15:19,799
I still have to tend to our parents' graves for you.

232
00:15:21,720 --> 00:15:25,840
Father and Mother are waiting for you.

233
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:28,080
They're waiting for you, Brother!

234
00:15:28,519 --> 00:15:30,039
Why didn't you come back?

235
00:15:30,039 --> 00:15:33,600
Why didn't you come back?

236
00:15:40,799 --> 00:15:43,000
Brother!

237
00:15:49,480 --> 00:15:50,159
Great-Grandfather,

238
00:15:50,480 --> 00:15:51,759
your descendants have come to visit you.

239
00:15:52,240 --> 00:15:53,399
Look, this is Lin Kanshan.

240
00:15:53,919 --> 00:15:54,960
He is your great-grandson.

241
00:16:13,320 --> 00:16:15,799
This whole area belongs to our family.

242
00:16:15,919 --> 00:16:18,720
From here to over there, it's all Lin family land.

243
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:20,279
I'm a nephew; my surname is Chen.

244
00:16:21,919 --> 00:16:23,240
It looks pretty clean.

245
00:16:23,879 --> 00:16:26,039
Do people often come to clean it?

246
00:16:26,039 --> 00:16:27,200
The neighbors do.

247
00:16:27,200 --> 00:16:28,799
Whoever comes by helps tidy up.

248
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:30,240
We're all Hakka people.

249
00:16:30,480 --> 00:16:31,480
Your grandfather was too.

250
00:16:31,480 --> 00:16:33,159
And you folks living in Taiwan, China.

251
00:16:33,279 --> 00:16:36,000
We originally migrated from the Central Plains.

252
00:16:36,159 --> 00:16:37,639
This tradition of looking out for each other...

253
00:16:37,679 --> 00:16:38,600
goes without saying.

254
00:16:38,960 --> 00:16:40,440
It's the same wherever we go.

255
00:16:43,240 --> 00:16:43,840
Cousin...

256
00:16:44,279 --> 00:16:45,720
as for tomb-sweeping times,

257
00:16:45,720 --> 00:16:47,000
are there any specific rules?

258
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:48,840
My dad told me to come visit more often.

259
00:16:48,840 --> 00:16:50,200
I'm your uncle, actually.

260
00:16:50,480 --> 00:16:52,759
Even so, I won't be able to make many trips.

261
00:16:53,039 --> 00:16:54,159
Whenever!

262
00:16:54,399 --> 00:16:56,519
Just come back whenever you want.

263
00:17:02,360 --> 00:17:02,799
Excuse me.

264
00:17:02,799 --> 00:17:03,799
I need to take this call.

265
00:17:03,960 --> 00:17:04,799
I understand.

266
00:17:05,480 --> 00:17:07,000
I understand. I know it's hard.

267
00:17:20,920 --> 00:17:22,880
16 kilometers southwest of Gulou District,

268
00:17:22,880 --> 00:17:24,519
next to the dual-use airport,

269
00:17:24,519 --> 00:17:25,640
there is a plot of industrial land.

270
00:17:25,640 --> 00:17:27,559
Find a way to acquire it. It'll be useful.

271
00:17:49,880 --> 00:17:51,680
Here, eat some more eggs.

272
00:17:57,559 --> 00:17:58,240
Look at you...

273
00:17:58,240 --> 00:17:59,640
You're done after eating so little?

274
00:18:01,119 --> 00:18:02,319
Look at this kid.

275
00:18:02,880 --> 00:18:05,440
I just gave him food, and he won't touch a bite.

276
00:18:06,160 --> 00:18:08,519
Stop treating him like a child.

277
00:18:10,680 --> 00:18:11,759
He won't starve.

278
00:18:12,720 --> 00:18:15,200
From now on, just take care of yourself.

279
00:18:15,359 --> 00:18:16,440
You too.

280
00:18:16,440 --> 00:18:17,759
You're not young anymore,

281
00:18:18,240 --> 00:18:20,240
yet you still work yourself to the bone like a youngster.

282
00:18:20,680 --> 00:18:22,960
What good is sacrificing your life for the martyrs' shrine?

283
00:18:22,960 --> 00:18:24,599
Zheng Guiping will just come by,

284
00:18:24,599 --> 00:18:26,680
say a few hypocritical words,

285
00:18:26,680 --> 00:18:28,079
bow once, and leave.

286
00:18:28,079 --> 00:18:29,680
The moment he steps out, he'll forget all about you.

287
00:18:29,680 --> 00:18:30,440
Here.

288
00:18:30,599 --> 00:18:31,960
Have some mung bean soup.

289
00:18:32,279 --> 00:18:33,799
I put rock sugar in it.

290
00:18:33,799 --> 00:18:35,599
Why are you so worked up?

291
00:18:36,759 --> 00:18:38,359
Tell me, you haven't even retired yet,

292
00:18:40,519 --> 00:18:41,960
so why are the higher-ups giving so much work

293
00:18:41,960 --> 00:18:43,000
to Chen Leyuan?

294
00:18:43,319 --> 00:18:45,240
Will Lin Kanshan have to take orders from him too?

295
00:18:45,599 --> 00:18:47,440
Other than kissing up to people,

296
00:18:47,440 --> 00:18:48,519
what else can he do?

297
00:18:48,799 --> 00:18:52,000
It's because you only know how to work, not play politics.

298
00:18:52,279 --> 00:18:54,759
If brown-nosing is all that counts now,

299
00:18:54,759 --> 00:18:56,920
then the MIB is doomed too.

300
00:18:57,200 --> 00:18:59,599
My tooth started aching again these past couple of days.

301
00:19:00,839 --> 00:19:01,839
Can't be bothered to go to the hospital.

302
00:19:01,839 --> 00:19:04,200
Go buy me some anti-inflammatories, will you?

303
00:19:05,039 --> 00:19:05,960
Anti-inflammatories?

304
00:19:05,960 --> 00:19:08,359
Chen Leyuan is your rotten tooth!

305
00:19:08,359 --> 00:19:09,839
If you don't pull him out,

306
00:19:09,839 --> 00:19:11,359
just wait for the pain to get worse.

307
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:13,880
Lately, rumors say your health is failing,

308
00:19:14,119 --> 00:19:16,079
and that you even pick up your checkups secretly.

309
00:19:16,640 --> 00:19:18,000
Did he make that up?

310
00:19:18,359 --> 00:19:19,319
It must be him.

311
00:19:19,440 --> 00:19:22,279
Young men want to get ahead. It's normal.

312
00:19:24,680 --> 00:19:26,559
Rumors stop with the superiors.

313
00:19:26,559 --> 00:19:29,000
Zheng Guiping has spent his whole life in officialdom,

314
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:30,039
yet he won't say a single word for you.

315
00:19:30,039 --> 00:19:31,319
What's his angle?

316
00:19:33,119 --> 00:19:33,920
Who knows how many big messes

317
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:35,400
he has to deal with right now?

318
00:19:35,400 --> 00:19:36,799
How could he bother with petty stuff like this?

319
00:19:36,799 --> 00:19:38,599
Isn't it just Ma Qi?

320
00:19:41,039 --> 00:19:42,319
You brought him over,

321
00:19:42,480 --> 00:19:43,319
met with him,

322
00:19:43,440 --> 00:19:44,720
and had drinks together.

323
00:19:44,720 --> 00:19:46,559
All the intel to be bought or traded was handed over.

324
00:19:46,559 --> 00:19:48,400
What more does he want?

325
00:19:49,799 --> 00:19:51,559
When it comes to putting your life on the line,

326
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:53,039
it's never that easy.

327
00:19:53,279 --> 00:19:55,640
Zheng Guiping has tasted every fine dish out there.

328
00:19:56,119 --> 00:19:57,960
Whether Ma Qi is a good cook,

329
00:19:57,960 --> 00:19:59,000
where his true loyalties lie,

330
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,079
whether he's two-faced,

331
00:20:00,480 --> 00:20:01,799
or if he's just a fraud...

332
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:03,240
That remains to be seen.

333
00:20:17,599 --> 00:20:19,000
Lao Jia just gave me this.

334
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:19,920
I've sorted it all out.

335
00:20:19,920 --> 00:20:20,680
Take care of it.

336
00:20:26,440 --> 00:20:27,200
Put out that cigarette.

337
00:20:27,599 --> 00:20:28,440
How many times do I have to tell you?

338
00:20:35,759 --> 00:20:36,400
Time to eat.

339
00:21:07,839 --> 00:21:09,079
It's become a habit.

340
00:21:09,640 --> 00:21:11,000
I keep thinking I'm still in prison.

341
00:21:11,359 --> 00:21:12,920
Once chopsticks touch my mouth, I don't dare stop.

342
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:16,480
Luckily, Master Qi had someone look after me,

343
00:21:16,599 --> 00:21:18,079
otherwise who knows how much I'd have suffered.

344
00:21:18,480 --> 00:21:20,559
Professor Cao, you can really endure.

345
00:21:20,640 --> 00:21:21,319
You can take any hardship.

346
00:21:21,319 --> 00:21:22,440
And you're still staying quiet.

347
00:21:23,039 --> 00:21:24,759
Why bother talking about pointless things?

348
00:21:25,079 --> 00:21:26,240
I'm not afraid of anything else,

349
00:21:26,640 --> 00:21:27,839
I just dread this toothache.

350
00:21:28,359 --> 00:21:29,079
Periodontitis.

351
00:21:29,480 --> 00:21:31,440
Can't fill it, can't pull it.

352
00:21:31,839 --> 00:21:32,640
If I pull it,

353
00:21:32,640 --> 00:21:33,880
this whole row has to come out.

354
00:21:33,880 --> 00:21:35,160
They say a toothache isn't an illness,

355
00:21:35,160 --> 00:21:36,279
but the pain can kill you.

356
00:21:36,519 --> 00:21:37,240
It really does.

357
00:21:37,400 --> 00:21:39,359
The pain keeps me awake all night long.

358
00:21:39,480 --> 00:21:40,359
Don't even mention it.

359
00:21:40,359 --> 00:21:42,200
So hurry up and eat,

360
00:21:42,920 --> 00:21:43,960
hurry up and make money.

361
00:21:43,960 --> 00:21:44,759
Got it?

362
00:21:45,839 --> 00:21:48,519
We'll swap them all for porcelain crowns later. Get to work.

363
00:21:50,960 --> 00:21:54,319
I heard porcelain teeth must be replaced every 15 years.

364
00:21:54,920 --> 00:21:56,200
Not sure if that's true.

365
00:21:57,880 --> 00:21:58,839
We don't even know what'll happen next year,

366
00:21:58,839 --> 00:21:59,960
and you're thinking 15 years ahead?

367
00:23:10,200 --> 00:23:11,400
It's very well written.

368
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:12,599
What are you feeling guilty about?

369
00:23:12,839 --> 00:23:13,440
I'm not.

370
00:23:14,240 --> 00:23:14,839
I'm not feeling guilty.

371
00:23:14,839 --> 00:23:15,519
Ever since I walked in,

372
00:23:15,519 --> 00:23:16,680
you've been acting evasive.

373
00:23:16,920 --> 00:23:17,519
Look at me.

374
00:23:18,359 --> 00:23:20,759
That's it. I'm not a prison boss, what's to fear?

375
00:23:20,759 --> 00:23:22,039
You used to lie with such confidence.

376
00:23:22,039 --> 00:23:23,599
How come you've lost your nerve now?

377
00:23:23,960 --> 00:23:26,599
The intelligence that I analyzed myself

378
00:23:27,039 --> 00:23:28,279
is definitely solid.

379
00:23:28,960 --> 00:23:29,759
Then what is it?

380
00:23:30,440 --> 00:23:32,079
The parts I told you to fabricate make you uneasy?

381
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:38,119
It's like this, Brother Qi.

382
00:23:38,119 --> 00:23:39,440
What I deduced myself,

383
00:23:39,440 --> 00:23:41,599
I'm confident about, from the logic to the chain.

384
00:23:41,599 --> 00:23:43,200
Backwards and forwards,

385
00:23:43,200 --> 00:23:44,079
it all checks out.

386
00:23:44,079 --> 00:23:46,559
But when national leaders inspect the provinces,

387
00:23:46,559 --> 00:23:47,759
or visit Hong Kong, China,

388
00:23:47,759 --> 00:23:48,799
who goes ahead to scout,

389
00:23:48,799 --> 00:23:49,759
how they inspect the hotels,

390
00:23:49,759 --> 00:23:50,880
and how they take precautions—

391
00:23:50,880 --> 00:23:52,039
I really don't understand any of that.

392
00:23:52,519 --> 00:23:53,960
I don't know how to fabricate the details.

393
00:23:55,000 --> 00:23:56,200
I'm certainly not afraid.

394
00:23:56,400 --> 00:23:57,960
I just worry Taiwan, China will see through it.

395
00:23:58,519 --> 00:23:59,880
What is intelligence?

396
00:24:00,319 --> 00:24:01,920
It's always been a blend of truth and lies.

397
00:24:02,279 --> 00:24:04,440
The things that seem completely made up

398
00:24:04,440 --> 00:24:07,279
are actually things that really happened.

399
00:24:07,279 --> 00:24:09,839
While information that seems airtight

400
00:24:09,839 --> 00:24:11,480
will instead leave traces of fabrication.

401
00:24:12,039 --> 00:24:12,799
Intelligence work

402
00:24:12,799 --> 00:24:13,759
isn't just about information.

403
00:24:14,200 --> 00:24:15,000
It's also about handling people.

404
00:24:15,279 --> 00:24:18,039
In Taiwan, China, the MIB and the National Security Bureau

405
00:24:18,039 --> 00:24:20,200
also compete over merits and intel assets.

406
00:24:20,480 --> 00:24:22,519
Neither side respects the other.

407
00:24:22,519 --> 00:24:23,440
As for the MIB,

408
00:24:23,440 --> 00:24:24,920
it belongs to the so-called "Ministry of National Defense."

409
00:24:24,920 --> 00:24:27,240
They have more money, better merits, and faster promotions.

410
00:24:27,240 --> 00:24:28,960
The National Security Bureau is far worse off.

411
00:24:29,160 --> 00:24:30,160
Neither will yield to the other.

412
00:24:31,920 --> 00:24:34,359
So we leak all of this out:

413
00:24:34,359 --> 00:24:35,359
the real intel to the MIB,

414
00:24:35,960 --> 00:24:38,039
and the fake intel to the National Security Bureau.

415
00:24:38,039 --> 00:24:39,279
You get what I mean?

416
00:24:39,279 --> 00:24:42,559
Help a friend, take down a rival.

417
00:24:44,480 --> 00:24:45,279
Sit.

418
00:24:48,279 --> 00:24:50,480
I always thought you were an idealist.

419
00:24:50,480 --> 00:24:51,839
Someone who couldn't make money,

420
00:24:51,839 --> 00:24:52,880
wouldn't help a friend,

421
00:24:52,880 --> 00:24:53,880
and wouldn't undermine a rival.

422
00:24:53,880 --> 00:24:56,039
How did just a few years in prison

423
00:24:56,039 --> 00:24:57,079
suddenly open your eyes?

424
00:25:01,680 --> 00:25:03,279
When I first went inside,

425
00:25:04,640 --> 00:25:06,000
I constantly felt wronged.

426
00:25:06,000 --> 00:25:07,480
I had earned credit for my cooperation.

427
00:25:07,480 --> 00:25:09,200
I handed over all the materials.

428
00:25:09,200 --> 00:25:11,839
So why lock me up for so long?

429
00:25:12,240 --> 00:25:14,200
An older guy happened to be locked up next door.

430
00:25:14,480 --> 00:25:15,759
He felt wronged too.

431
00:25:15,759 --> 00:25:17,319
He said, "I turned myself in,

432
00:25:17,319 --> 00:25:19,160
so why did you still sentence me to death?"

433
00:25:19,920 --> 00:25:20,720
Do you know?

434
00:25:20,960 --> 00:25:23,000
When a person learns their fate,

435
00:25:24,359 --> 00:25:25,599
in those final few days,

436
00:25:27,920 --> 00:25:30,160
the look in his eyes and his face

437
00:25:30,160 --> 00:25:31,359
change completely.

438
00:25:32,200 --> 00:25:33,440
It's like he becomes someone else.

439
00:25:34,359 --> 00:25:35,400
A few days later,

440
00:25:36,599 --> 00:25:37,720
he was executed by firing squad.

441
00:25:38,319 --> 00:25:39,599
The cell next to mine was empty.

442
00:25:39,920 --> 00:25:40,319
That morning,

443
00:25:40,319 --> 00:25:41,960
I heard firecrackers going off outside.

444
00:25:42,160 --> 00:25:43,680
Crackling and popping,

445
00:25:43,680 --> 00:25:44,559
they just kept going.

446
00:25:46,519 --> 00:25:48,559
It was his family sending him on his final journey.

447
00:26:01,279 --> 00:26:03,319
I don't know how to describe that feeling.

448
00:26:03,920 --> 00:26:05,640
But ever since that day,

449
00:26:05,640 --> 00:26:06,680
I told myself,

450
00:26:07,240 --> 00:26:08,720
if I could get out alive,

451
00:26:10,480 --> 00:26:11,759
I'd hold on to life,

452
00:26:12,039 --> 00:26:13,039
live with all my might,

453
00:26:13,160 --> 00:26:14,279
and live well.

454
00:26:14,799 --> 00:26:16,400
I had to treat myself better,

455
00:26:18,559 --> 00:26:19,440
even better.

456
00:26:21,640 --> 00:26:23,480
So if you weren't working with me,

457
00:26:24,200 --> 00:26:25,559
you'd be working for someone else?

458
00:26:29,240 --> 00:26:30,079
Not necessarily.

459
00:26:32,240 --> 00:26:33,839
Anyone else would have to pay more.

460
00:26:59,160 --> 00:27:00,640
I'm hungry too.

461
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:03,000
I'll make a bowl of noodles.

462
00:27:14,640 --> 00:27:17,079
So, did your neighbor get up during the night?

463
00:27:19,359 --> 00:27:21,400
I remember when I first came here,

464
00:27:21,400 --> 00:27:24,079
listening to him, he could sleep through the night.

465
00:27:24,079 --> 00:27:26,720
Now he gets up several times a night,

466
00:27:26,720 --> 00:27:28,240
and wakes up earlier and earlier.

467
00:27:28,519 --> 00:27:29,839
He's not even 40 yet.

468
00:27:29,839 --> 00:27:31,640
How did his sleep get as bad as mine?

469
00:27:32,039 --> 00:27:32,960
He has a lot on his mind.

470
00:27:33,160 --> 00:27:34,559
Never knowing what day he'll wake up

471
00:27:34,559 --> 00:27:36,079
to another mission from Taiwan, China.

472
00:27:36,559 --> 00:27:38,559
With two neighbors next door who don don't sleep,

473
00:27:38,720 --> 00:27:40,759
it's pretty good that he can even doze off.

474
00:27:41,079 --> 00:27:44,240
What about you? Still having vivid, chaotic dreams?

475
00:27:44,240 --> 00:27:45,880
The Chinese herbal medicine actually helped.

476
00:27:46,440 --> 00:27:47,559
Though I sleep less,

477
00:27:47,559 --> 00:27:48,680
it's much deeper.

478
00:27:49,960 --> 00:27:52,759
Say, if one day we get a call from above

479
00:27:52,960 --> 00:27:54,680
telling us to go next door and make the arrest,

480
00:27:54,680 --> 00:27:55,480
no more waiting,

481
00:27:55,759 --> 00:27:57,440
and they tell you to take time off,

482
00:27:57,440 --> 00:27:58,920
no need to worry about the wiretap anymore...

483
00:27:58,920 --> 00:28:00,599
Do you think you'd sleep more soundly,

484
00:28:00,599 --> 00:28:01,960
or feel an empty void?

485
00:28:02,640 --> 00:28:03,839
I heard Baoshan say

486
00:28:04,559 --> 00:28:06,119
that when Old Wei was young,

487
00:28:06,359 --> 00:28:08,319
he also monitored someone from Taiwan, China.

488
00:28:08,319 --> 00:28:10,279
For 17 years in total.

489
00:28:10,279 --> 00:28:12,240
Not only were their families neighbors,

490
00:28:12,240 --> 00:28:14,680
they were even distant relatives.

491
00:28:14,680 --> 00:28:15,720
The kids from both families

492
00:28:15,720 --> 00:28:17,359
went to the same school, too.

493
00:28:17,359 --> 00:28:18,559
On the day of the arrest,

494
00:28:18,559 --> 00:28:21,480
Old Wei thought he'd be thrilled and laugh.

495
00:28:22,279 --> 00:28:23,400
Nobody expected

496
00:28:24,119 --> 00:28:25,079
that he actually broke down and cried.

497
00:28:28,880 --> 00:28:30,319
It's like running a marathon.

498
00:28:30,319 --> 00:28:31,759
It's unimaginably hard,

499
00:28:31,759 --> 00:28:33,000
and you never stop.

500
00:28:33,559 --> 00:28:34,920
You get so used to running

501
00:28:34,920 --> 00:28:37,319
that reaching the finish line leaves you feeling lost.

502
00:28:37,319 --> 00:28:38,400
I wouldn't feel lost.

503
00:28:38,799 --> 00:28:40,319
If the day of the arrest really comes,

504
00:28:40,519 --> 00:28:42,160
I'll definitely be celebrating big time.

505
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:52,799
Try this.

506
00:29:00,079 --> 00:29:00,960
As time goes on,

507
00:29:02,160 --> 00:29:03,519
many things become a weight on your mind.

508
00:29:04,000 --> 00:29:05,759
Take that old codebook, for example.

509
00:29:05,759 --> 00:29:07,160
Fourteen years have passed, and it's still missing.

510
00:29:07,480 --> 00:29:10,079
Even though comms are now encrypted,

511
00:29:10,079 --> 00:29:11,920
if we could crack that cipher,

512
00:29:11,920 --> 00:29:13,160
we could still examine the link

513
00:29:13,160 --> 00:29:14,599
between the codebook and the coded cables,

514
00:29:14,880 --> 00:29:16,160
and tie them back to past cases.

515
00:29:17,720 --> 00:29:18,599
Let me tell you,

516
00:29:18,960 --> 00:29:20,400
with things like this, all you can do is wait.

517
00:29:20,599 --> 00:29:21,799
Just like when you're

518
00:29:21,799 --> 00:29:23,920
desperately looking for nail clippers in a drawer,

519
00:29:24,400 --> 00:29:26,119
you search everywhere and can't find them.

520
00:29:26,119 --> 00:29:27,400
Then, once you don't need them anymore,

521
00:29:27,720 --> 00:29:29,799
they suddenly turn up out of nowhere.

522
00:29:30,920 --> 00:29:31,720
Wait?

523
00:29:33,480 --> 00:29:34,960
We might as well wait until retirement.

524
00:29:35,880 --> 00:29:37,160
I asked Old Wei the other day.

525
00:29:37,400 --> 00:29:39,680
I said we have enough evidence,

526
00:29:39,680 --> 00:29:40,680
so when do we make the arrest?

527
00:29:40,920 --> 00:29:42,400
He said you have to read the man first.

528
00:29:42,720 --> 00:29:44,160
A man like Lin Kanshan...

529
00:29:44,160 --> 00:29:45,359
he chases petty gains,

530
00:29:45,359 --> 00:29:46,720
but he has a sense of a greater cause.

531
00:29:47,119 --> 00:29:48,279
He feels goodwill toward the mainland, too.

532
00:29:48,279 --> 00:29:49,559
So we need to keep him on the hook

533
00:29:49,920 --> 00:29:50,880
and turn him.

534
00:29:52,240 --> 00:29:53,200
He's so slippery.

535
00:29:53,599 --> 00:29:55,039
Are we sure we can turn him?

536
00:29:55,640 --> 00:29:56,920
That's hard to say.

537
00:29:57,920 --> 00:30:00,119
If he's willing, we have to show good faith.

538
00:30:00,319 --> 00:30:01,240
Making friends...

539
00:30:01,720 --> 00:30:02,839
it's never too late.

540
00:30:03,559 --> 00:30:04,799
So do we arrest him or not?

541
00:30:10,519 --> 00:30:11,599
Protect his cover,

542
00:30:12,000 --> 00:30:13,039
show him ample respect...

543
00:30:13,359 --> 00:30:14,960
Covert arrest is also a form of understanding.

544
00:30:15,240 --> 00:30:16,400
Just wait for word.

545
00:30:23,079 --> 00:30:24,880
How were your checkup results today?

546
00:30:24,880 --> 00:30:25,880
Is your gastritis any better?

547
00:30:26,599 --> 00:30:27,400
Same as always.

548
00:30:28,119 --> 00:30:29,680
They said I've got another ulcer.

549
00:30:29,680 --> 00:30:31,079
Not that I feel anything, anyway.

550
00:30:31,079 --> 00:30:33,599
What about you? Did your hyperthyroidism ease up?

551
00:30:35,119 --> 00:30:36,759
It swung into hypothyroidism last time.

552
00:30:37,240 --> 00:30:38,480
Still trying to balance it out.

553
00:30:38,880 --> 00:30:40,119
My blood pressure is a bit high.

554
00:30:41,240 --> 00:30:43,599
Since when do you have high blood pressure?

555
00:30:43,599 --> 00:30:46,519
Was your heart racing last time because of that?

556
00:30:48,680 --> 00:30:50,799
How long has it been since we talked like this?

557
00:30:52,400 --> 00:30:53,640
A year?

558
00:30:53,640 --> 00:30:54,200
Has it?

559
00:30:55,480 --> 00:30:56,480
Has it really been that long?

560
00:30:59,039 --> 00:31:00,079
I can hardly remember.

561
00:31:02,440 --> 00:31:04,039
When I saw Director Wu last time,

562
00:31:05,359 --> 00:31:07,359
his eyes were completely bloodshot.

563
00:31:07,359 --> 00:31:08,519
They were totally red.

564
00:31:08,759 --> 00:31:10,759
He said high blood pressure does that.

565
00:31:11,359 --> 00:31:12,799
So you must take your medication on time.

566
00:31:14,160 --> 00:31:16,200
I ran into Uncle Wu on the street the other day.

567
00:31:16,200 --> 00:31:17,559
Looking at him from afar,

568
00:31:17,559 --> 00:31:19,079
why has he aged so much?

569
00:31:20,000 --> 00:31:21,319
His hair has gone completely gray.

570
00:31:21,319 --> 00:31:23,319
The mental and physical toll is immense.

571
00:31:23,720 --> 00:31:24,799
The stress is heavy, too.

572
00:31:24,799 --> 00:31:27,519
Internal security checks are so frequent.

573
00:31:27,519 --> 00:31:29,559
They say a clear conscience fears no knock,

574
00:31:29,880 --> 00:31:31,960
but no one can take a knock on the door every day.

575
00:31:32,319 --> 00:31:34,160
Everyone is visibly aging.

576
00:31:35,079 --> 00:31:35,880
What about me?

577
00:31:36,359 --> 00:31:37,400
Have I gotten old, too?

578
00:31:39,400 --> 00:31:40,160
Hold still.

579
00:31:51,599 --> 00:31:52,480
You have wrinkles too.

580
00:31:52,480 --> 00:31:54,480
Do I? Where?

581
00:31:54,480 --> 00:31:55,480
On my face or around my eyes?

582
00:31:55,480 --> 00:31:56,759
Looks like it's...

583
00:31:57,279 --> 00:31:58,240
On your nose.

584
00:31:58,240 --> 00:31:59,079
My nose?

585
00:32:26,200 --> 00:32:27,079
Old Wei.

586
00:32:30,440 --> 00:32:31,240
Chief Wei.

587
00:32:33,720 --> 00:32:34,720
There's a new assignment.

588
00:32:36,319 --> 00:32:37,119
When do we leave?

589
00:32:41,759 --> 00:32:43,759
Okay, got it.

590
00:32:48,960 --> 00:32:51,640
Brother Wen, you've got to be kidding.

591
00:32:52,640 --> 00:32:54,039
A lazy guy like me...

592
00:32:54,039 --> 00:32:55,559
How could I ever be secretary-general?

593
00:32:56,440 --> 00:32:58,119
I'm fine just being your assistant.

594
00:33:01,960 --> 00:33:03,759
What kind of person is a secretary-general?

595
00:33:04,839 --> 00:33:06,720
Slick and tactful, juggling everything inside and out.

596
00:33:06,720 --> 00:33:08,079
Someone with plenty of money and leisure.

597
00:33:08,839 --> 00:33:10,039
I'm not just being modest.

598
00:33:10,039 --> 00:33:11,279
I really can't do it.

599
00:33:11,279 --> 00:33:12,240
I don't have what it takes.

600
00:33:12,240 --> 00:33:14,559
Just give me orders whenever you need something.

601
00:33:16,480 --> 00:33:17,920
Even deputy is out of the question.

602
00:33:17,920 --> 00:33:19,079
I really can't pull it off.

603
00:33:19,079 --> 00:33:20,720
Alright, alright. We'll talk about it later.

604
00:33:21,480 --> 00:33:22,720
Okay, okay.

605
00:33:23,440 --> 00:33:24,240
Boss.

606
00:33:24,680 --> 00:33:27,519
Two contracts need your stamp and signature.

607
00:33:30,440 --> 00:33:31,240
What is this?

608
00:33:31,559 --> 00:33:32,319
Ox bezoar.

609
00:33:34,160 --> 00:33:35,440
Ox bezoar?

610
00:33:35,440 --> 00:33:36,680
Gallstones from cattle.

611
00:33:38,720 --> 00:33:40,480
If this stuff is authentic,

612
00:33:40,480 --> 00:33:41,920
it could fetch hundreds of thousands at auction.

613
00:33:42,319 --> 00:33:43,279
Where did you get it?

614
00:33:43,279 --> 00:33:44,319
My grandma gave it to me.

615
00:33:44,599 --> 00:33:45,680
Before she passed away,

616
00:33:45,720 --> 00:33:47,960
I went to visit her, and she slipped it to me.

617
00:33:47,960 --> 00:33:49,359
She said it was a family heirloom,

618
00:33:49,359 --> 00:33:50,880
meant to help me land a job.

619
00:33:50,880 --> 00:33:51,480
If she knew

620
00:33:51,480 --> 00:33:53,160
I have this iron rice bowl now,

621
00:33:53,160 --> 00:33:54,319
she'd be smiling in her grave.

622
00:33:55,319 --> 00:33:57,319
Don't give such a treasure to Wu Jinhe.

623
00:33:57,319 --> 00:33:58,960
I've done him countless favors.

624
00:33:58,960 --> 00:34:00,720
Getting him to arrange a post at the arts federation

625
00:34:00,720 --> 00:34:02,279
takes zero effort on his part.

626
00:34:02,839 --> 00:34:03,960
It's not for him.

627
00:34:04,359 --> 00:34:05,480
It's for your dad.

628
00:34:05,480 --> 00:34:07,079
He's getting on in years. It wards off bad luck.

629
00:34:12,320 --> 00:34:13,880
Working at his place,

630
00:34:13,880 --> 00:34:16,559
doing nothing and drawing a ghost salary—

631
00:34:16,559 --> 00:34:17,760
could that cause trouble?

632
00:34:17,960 --> 00:34:20,519
Do you think I should give

633
00:34:20,519 --> 00:34:22,280
a gift to the arts federation chair?

634
00:34:22,280 --> 00:34:23,079
No need.

635
00:34:23,960 --> 00:34:25,480
You're a poet, after all.

636
00:34:25,480 --> 00:34:26,960
When do poets ever report to an office?

637
00:34:26,960 --> 00:34:27,800
You deserve the spot.

638
00:34:28,239 --> 00:34:29,440
Nobody writes better than you.

639
00:34:29,719 --> 00:34:31,679
How many of my poems have you even read

640
00:34:31,960 --> 00:34:33,159
to say I'm that good?

641
00:34:33,159 --> 00:34:35,360
You kidding? I've read plenty.

642
00:34:35,880 --> 00:34:37,559
Isn't it all in that little notebook

643
00:34:37,559 --> 00:34:38,760
lying on the desk?

644
00:34:38,760 --> 00:34:41,119
Autumn, falling leaves,

645
00:34:41,119 --> 00:34:42,960
life and death,

646
00:34:42,960 --> 00:34:44,440
tears one minute, laughter the next...

647
00:34:44,719 --> 00:34:45,639
Isn't that what's in there?

648
00:34:47,079 --> 00:34:48,320
Have some faith in yourself.

649
00:34:48,320 --> 00:34:49,079
No problem at all.

650
00:34:51,519 --> 00:34:53,119
The people seeking sponsorships the other day—

651
00:34:53,119 --> 00:34:54,480
where's that brochure?

652
00:34:55,320 --> 00:34:56,559
Which one do you mean?

653
00:34:56,559 --> 00:34:57,320
The fishing contest,

654
00:34:57,320 --> 00:34:59,159
or the stadium billboard?

655
00:34:59,159 --> 00:35:00,639
What about the book by the CPPCC?

656
00:35:00,639 --> 00:35:03,320
And the Cultural and Historical Data Committee?

657
00:35:03,320 --> 00:35:04,960
Memoirs of Taiwan, China veterans' families.

658
00:35:04,960 --> 00:35:05,719
I want to sponsor this one.

659
00:35:05,920 --> 00:35:06,719
They're all over here.

660
00:35:18,199 --> 00:35:19,239
All right.

661
00:35:19,239 --> 00:35:19,880
Understood.

662
00:35:22,519 --> 00:35:25,159
Go to my place and get something for me.

663
00:35:25,159 --> 00:35:26,360
Call me once you get there.

664
00:35:26,360 --> 00:35:27,320
I'll tell you where it is.

665
00:35:27,320 --> 00:35:28,159
Okay.

666
00:36:24,880 --> 00:36:27,000
How can we tell which one is the codebook?

667
00:36:29,360 --> 00:36:30,480
First, look at the books.

668
00:36:30,800 --> 00:36:32,519
Which one has clearly

669
00:36:32,519 --> 00:36:34,079
and frequently been taken down?

670
00:36:34,079 --> 00:36:34,960
The more it's flipped through,

671
00:36:35,199 --> 00:36:37,079
the more a new book turns worn.

672
00:36:45,440 --> 00:36:46,440
Next, look at the covers.

673
00:36:46,679 --> 00:36:47,880
Some are very distinctive,

674
00:36:48,800 --> 00:36:50,159
maybe unconventional,

675
00:36:50,480 --> 00:36:52,280
maybe rarely seen.

676
00:36:52,599 --> 00:36:53,920
See which books

677
00:36:53,920 --> 00:36:56,079
clash with Lin Kanshan's personality,

678
00:36:56,280 --> 00:36:58,599
or stray far from his usual reading habits.

679
00:36:59,000 --> 00:37:00,239
Which ones seem out of place?

680
00:37:00,679 --> 00:37:01,480
Which books

681
00:37:01,480 --> 00:37:03,480
are beyond Lin Kanshan's education level?

682
00:37:03,800 --> 00:37:04,960
Focus your search on those.

683
00:37:05,119 --> 00:37:05,840
Look closely.

684
00:37:05,880 --> 00:37:06,719
Think it through.

685
00:37:06,840 --> 00:37:07,679
Use your head.

686
00:37:08,400 --> 00:37:09,880
Put yourself in his shoes.

687
00:37:10,360 --> 00:37:11,840
See which book he would reach for.

688
00:37:12,239 --> 00:37:13,519
Maybe you can't imagine it.

689
00:37:14,599 --> 00:37:16,280
You also have to check the marks on the books.

690
00:37:16,760 --> 00:37:18,239
Which ones have folded pages?

691
00:37:18,960 --> 00:37:19,960
The more folds there are,

692
00:37:20,400 --> 00:37:21,519
the more attention you must pay.

693
00:37:44,599 --> 00:37:45,639
Why are you back?

694
00:37:46,000 --> 00:37:47,440
Coming back to my own home,

695
00:37:47,440 --> 00:37:49,000
do I have to report to you?

696
00:38:11,239 --> 00:38:12,320
I'm already home.

697
00:38:12,639 --> 00:38:14,840
Yeah, I was afraid we'd run out of time.

698
00:38:15,679 --> 00:38:17,400
I'll grab it here and bring it over.

699
00:38:17,800 --> 00:38:20,079
Let's stick with that teahouse north of People's Park.

700
00:38:20,800 --> 00:38:22,119
It's closer from here.

701
00:38:22,800 --> 00:38:23,639
All right.

702
00:38:24,119 --> 00:38:25,840
Then I'll wait at home for your driver.

703
00:38:26,440 --> 00:38:27,239
No problem.

704
00:38:30,400 --> 00:38:32,760
Your bookcase is a total mess.

705
00:38:33,039 --> 00:38:34,320
Want me to help you organize it?

706
00:38:34,599 --> 00:38:35,760
Why even ask?

707
00:38:37,320 --> 00:38:39,079
Haven't you already organized it?

708
00:38:39,800 --> 00:38:41,039
Everything is in the wrong spot.

709
00:38:41,599 --> 00:38:43,000
Did you think I wouldn't notice?

710
00:38:43,559 --> 00:38:46,280
I've been looking for Shu Ting's poetry collection.

711
00:38:46,280 --> 00:38:47,960
I saw it on the shelf before.

712
00:38:47,960 --> 00:38:48,679
Why is it gone?

713
00:38:48,679 --> 00:38:49,639
How should I know?

714
00:38:55,639 --> 00:38:57,159
Bought it at a secondhand bookstall.

715
00:38:57,159 --> 00:38:58,480
Just for show.

716
00:38:58,639 --> 00:38:59,719
I've never read it.

717
00:39:00,360 --> 00:39:01,559
If it's lost, so be it.

718
00:39:01,559 --> 00:39:05,119
Just don't lose my erotic novels.

719
00:39:05,119 --> 00:39:06,599
That's food for my soul.

720
00:39:13,320 --> 00:39:14,360
A philosophy book, huh?

721
00:39:15,000 --> 00:39:17,320
Nietzsche. Can you even understand it?

722
00:39:17,320 --> 00:39:18,079
You think my head

723
00:39:18,079 --> 00:39:19,920
has nothing in it except making money?

724
00:39:20,119 --> 00:39:21,880
If I don't put something in my head,

725
00:39:21,880 --> 00:39:23,360
how can I go out and talk big?

726
00:39:23,840 --> 00:39:25,440
After reading too much smut,

727
00:39:25,440 --> 00:39:28,199
reading this sometimes really strikes a chord.

728
00:39:30,559 --> 00:39:33,880
Everything in the world goes in cycles.

729
00:39:34,599 --> 00:39:38,199
One must face fate with a fearless heart.

730
00:39:39,559 --> 00:39:40,320
Get it?

731
00:39:42,400 --> 00:39:43,239
Scared yet?

732
00:40:01,920 --> 00:40:03,039
Then I'll wait for you at home.

733
00:40:04,079 --> 00:40:04,880
Okay.

734
00:40:11,519 --> 00:40:12,440
You head back first.

735
00:40:13,000 --> 00:40:14,559
Wu Jinhe is coming over to pick something up.

736
00:40:14,599 --> 00:40:16,079
He's been really paranoid lately.

737
00:40:17,079 --> 00:40:18,239
He doesn't want anyone to see him.

738
00:40:21,320 --> 00:40:22,400
I'll get going now.

739
00:40:26,800 --> 00:40:28,320
In a city this big,

740
00:40:29,440 --> 00:40:30,719
the only one I can trust,

741
00:40:30,960 --> 00:40:32,119
the only one I dare trust,

742
00:40:32,559 --> 00:40:34,000
is you.

743
00:40:34,800 --> 00:40:36,079
You won't betray me, will you?

744
00:40:37,960 --> 00:40:39,000
You won't hurt me,

745
00:40:39,599 --> 00:40:40,840
or lie to me, right?

746
00:40:52,159 --> 00:40:54,559
*Thus Spoke Zarathustra*, Nietzsche.

747
00:40:55,159 --> 00:40:57,000
Although the book looked brand-new,

748
00:40:57,400 --> 00:40:59,360
knowing him as I do,

749
00:41:00,239 --> 00:41:01,599
he wouldn't read philosophy.

750
00:41:02,159 --> 00:41:03,679
One page was heavily creased,

751
00:41:04,159 --> 00:41:06,719
and the first line on that page read:

752
00:41:07,199 --> 00:41:08,840
"What they cast at the hermit

753
00:41:10,440 --> 00:41:13,119
is injustice and filth.

754
00:41:13,800 --> 00:41:15,039
But, my brother,

755
00:41:15,639 --> 00:41:17,519
if you wish to be a star,

756
00:41:18,360 --> 00:41:20,800
you must still shine upon them."

757
00:41:26,679 --> 00:41:28,320
"If you wish to be a star,

758
00:41:28,679 --> 00:41:30,880
you must still shine upon them."

759
00:41:39,960 --> 00:41:41,920
I loved enoki mushrooms as a kid.

760
00:41:42,559 --> 00:41:44,760
Chewing them felt like both meat and veggies.

761
00:41:46,079 --> 00:41:48,800
My grandma said I was just craving meat.

762
00:41:49,320 --> 00:41:50,360
A huge pot like this—

763
00:41:51,360 --> 00:41:53,599
as a kid, it'd taste so good I'd swallow my tongue.

764
00:41:55,159 --> 00:41:56,599
Here, let me show you how to eat it.

765
00:41:58,280 --> 00:41:59,519
Dip it in a bit of seafood sauce,

766
00:41:59,519 --> 00:42:01,159
just a quick dip,

767
00:42:01,719 --> 00:42:03,079
and then coat it in chili flakes.

768
00:42:03,480 --> 00:42:05,360
That's the best way to eat enoki mushrooms.

769
00:42:28,239 --> 00:42:29,599
So spicy.

770
00:42:29,599 --> 00:42:31,239
It's the chili peppers.

771
00:42:39,400 --> 00:42:40,559
Something came up at work.

772
00:42:41,239 --> 00:42:43,239
I just got word I have to go out of town on business.

773
00:42:44,760 --> 00:42:45,880
Might be gone for a while.

774
00:42:58,239 --> 00:42:59,320
The next time we meet,

775
00:43:01,079 --> 00:43:02,360
it'll be someone else.

776
00:43:08,159 --> 00:43:08,760
Hello, everyone.

777
00:43:08,760 --> 00:43:10,480
I'm actress Zhou Yiran.

778
00:43:10,480 --> 00:43:12,119
Inviting you to watch the drama

779
00:43:12,119 --> 00:43:12,840
*Confrontation*.

780
00:43:12,880 --> 00:43:13,920
No matter how urgent it is,

781
00:43:13,920 --> 00:43:15,239
we can't contact each other anymore.

782
00:43:15,239 --> 00:43:16,000
Whatever you say.

783
00:43:16,000 --> 00:43:18,599
If you say no contact, then we won't.

784
00:43:18,599 --> 00:43:20,280
Can you hear what he's saying?

785
00:43:20,280 --> 00:43:21,159
The TV is too loud.

786
00:43:21,159 --> 00:43:22,400
I can't hear anything at all.

787
00:43:22,639 --> 00:43:24,079
Someone is watching you.

788
00:43:24,079 --> 00:43:26,440
Let's see if he has what it takes to catch me.

789
00:43:26,440 --> 00:43:28,079
First Lin Kanshan,

790
00:43:28,079 --> 00:43:29,400
and now Ma Qi.

791
00:43:29,400 --> 00:43:30,320
So many pieces in play,

792
00:43:30,320 --> 00:43:31,559
and the stakes are so high.

793
00:43:31,559 --> 00:43:32,480
Can we win?

794
00:43:32,480 --> 00:43:33,639
Be straight with me.

795
00:43:33,639 --> 00:43:34,800
What are you really trying to do?

796
00:43:35,599 --> 00:43:38,000
Wu Jinhe is going after Lin Kanshan.
